# Pre-Commit and Pre-Push Test Gate

Before any `git commit` or `git push`, run the full validation suites locally. CI must not be the first place tests run.

## Required checks

### Backend (requires Docker for Testcontainers)

```bash
mvn -B test
```

On Colima/macOS without `/var/run/docker.sock`, also set:

```bash
export DOCKER_HOST=unix://$HOME/.colima/default/docker.sock
export TESTCONTAINERS_RYUK_DISABLED=true
```

### Frontend (matches `.github/workflows/validate.yml`)

```bash
cd frontend && npm run lint && npx tsc --noEmit && npm run build
```

Set build env vars when needed:

```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1 \
API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8080 \
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://example.vercel.app \
NEXT_PUBLIC_IMAGE_CDN_HOST=d2568bpd35bq6a.cloudfront.net \
npm run build
```

## Rules

- Do **not** commit or push until **all** checks pass.
- If any test fails, fix the issue, re-run the full suites, then commit/push.
- Never skip hooks or push with known failing tests.
